    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "RRF adds reciprocal rank contributions from the input rankings; raw score magnitudes do not enter its formula. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://cormack.uwaterloo.ca/cormacksigir09-rrf.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0fb521627257bda2070ffc561045b0ef6b25a52a7a16369ab8d22061543243bd",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:158aa758d622a93663037c1fa984d2e3778129bc912983dc9df5c209d00a62ad"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In truncated-list RRF, an item absent from one input list contributes zero from that list. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/improving-information-retrieval-elastic-stack-hybrid",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6e072d2ba5fb4a212ee7e10b2b9f1fdc53aa9cc1781357514f9c997a260a1e43",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:99d0521c2e91157c424d89422be393dbaa97da938ccf32c629bf3df2288c34b6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Cormack et al. fixed k=60 during a pilot and retained it during later validation. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://cormack.uwaterloo.ca/cormacksigir09-rrf.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9e406e289d2bd68471be51538bd96dcaff7e162479fd0c8779607af20ae26c83",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:337554bd307d0d59ddea8b8c2d504a983fd44cdace288aae956c9ea304fd2be2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Elastic's 2023 BEIR subset experiment favored k=20 and candidate depth 1000 for the tested dense retrievers. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/improving-information-retrieval-elastic-stack-hybrid",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:46192c79ce857f7e4c69b1ecad7dcd15f11906aa3c19bb1a292f63b59c2f16ce",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:437181500bdaa37b87d54f7910f4292de6a7b183ce86693a22d5d9af3f203c43"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bruch et al. found tuned convex score combination superior to RRF in their in-domain and out-of-domain experiments. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://arxiv.org/html/2210.11934v2",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:626b3e49f1b956df7b97a557beb9e520750e0666d6ca91bae5ed80c7e02486fd",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1df2ed224afc6da590d6a4c7075ed0a941510b2e8c8a230816b0c9241677b037"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Elasticsearch separates the per-retriever rank window from the final response size. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-22)",
          "source": "https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/elasticsearch/rest-apis/reciprocal-rank-fusion",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b3a12ee0a931dbba43edb27a3f0e5ae05f0bec5e389ebbd8b064e281a95b426e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e00386f02e57e1f666ec25de2d0a8e746e01884218726f894efc677fd235a8dc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bruch et al.'s min-max normalization uses the minimum and maximum scores in the retrieved candidate union. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://arxiv.org/html/2210.11934v2",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a34986985e6ad987b3fa08dd2b49ef4732e1f13f3e5b3983041befafd52e1ab3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:74d6df16ae286a518b2352839b798d892b449bc1c86a8ec9cce35fb32a0f9ecf"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bruch et al. compute missing candidate scores and approximate otherwise unknown ranks within the candidate union. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://arxiv.org/html/2210.11934v2",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c3abada74bed2f9a2976c1ccae9631d602bd22e57cc2b1d039d7401225f288d4",
